<section class="section wrap" id="elder-law" aria-labelledby="elder-h">
  <h2 id="elder-h">Built for elder law, not borrowed from litigation software.</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">Most practice management tools are designed around litigation. DossierIQ starts from the work elder law firms actually do: gathering a lifetime of records, proving five years of statements, and finding the accounts nobody wrote down.</p>
  <div class="specifics">
    <div><b>The 60-month look-back</b><span>Coverage tracked by account and by month, so gaps show up before the caseworker finds them.</span></div>
    <div><b>Medicaid packet export</b><span>Documents grouped by checklist item, with a cover sheet listing what's included and what's still missing.</span></div>
    <div><b>How to get it</b><span>For each checklist item: who can ask for it, official sources and county links, and a draft request for your staff to review and send.</span></div>
    <div><b>Requests to the family</b><span>Ask for one missing item with an expiring upload link. What the family sends lands on that item for your staff to confirm.</span></div>
    <div><b>Your judgment stays in charge</b><span>DossierIQ organizes and flags; attorneys and staff confirm. It's guidance, not legal advice.</span></div>
    <div><b>Google Workspace and Microsoft 365</b><span>Keep documents in your firm's Google Drive or SharePoint, and sign in with a Google or Microsoft work account.</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="closing">Behind every file is a family trying to get it right.</p>
</section>

<section class="section wrap" id="digital-estate" aria-labelledby="digital-h">
  <h2 id="digital-h">The paper is only part of the picture.</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">Banking, investments, savings and insurance live in email inboxes and online portals as much as in shoeboxes.</p>
  <div class="feat feat-top">
    <div>
      <ul class="how">
        <li><b>Start with an email export.</b> After the firm records its authority, upload a client's export (Gmail Takeout, or any mailbox via Thunderbird). DossierIQ reads only account-related messages and builds an account map. Email bodies aren't stored.</li>
        <li><b>Attachments filed.</b> Statements and bills attached to those messages go to the matter's “Email attachments” folder and count toward the checklist and coverage. Family email isn't saved.</li>
        <li><b>Accounts and charges in one place.</b> Each account once, with its documents, and the recurring bills someone may need to stop, worked out from all of the matter's statements, not only the email.</li>
        <li><b>Leads become requests.</b> On a checklist item, “Look for leads” reads every document, emailed ones included, and lists clues with the document each came from.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="how-close">It helps your firm find what would otherwise be missed. It can't promise to find everything, and your team decides what matters.</p>
    </div>
